flowchart TB
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% K1 COGNITIVE KERNEL - ARCHITECTURE DIAGRAM
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% Updated: 2026-02-01 (Edge-First Design + Offline Awareness)
    %% Layers: L0-L6 + Cross-Kernel Bridge (bridge/) + IFL (bridge/ifl/) + Family Mesh
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% EDGE-FIRST DESIGN PRINCIPLE:
    %%   K1 is the brain. K0 is the library. The brain works even if the library is closed.
    %%   LOCAL COLD (K1 SQLite) = Device-local archive, always available
    %%   CLOUD SYNC (K0) = Optional enhancement for cross-device sync + long-term memory
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% K0 Integration: All K0 access via Cross-Kernel Bridge (security gateway)
    %% Bridge: Five responsibilities:
    %%   1. Kernel Transport (K0 ↔ K1 memory/storage)
    %%   2. Connector Security (Tools → External Devices via IFL)
    %%   3. Device Sync (Multi-device family sync via K0 P07)
    %%   4. IFL Ownership (Device Adapters - Homekit, Tesla, etc.)
    %%   5. Offline Awareness (K0HealthChecker, LocalOutbox, graceful degradation)
    %% See bridge/README.md for full Bridge architecture
    %% ======================================================================================

    %% ======================================================================================
    %% LLM CALL MATRIX - All MODEL_GATEWAY invocations with token budgets
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% | Consumer                    | Purpose                          | Tokens  | Priority    |
    %% |-----------------------------|----------------------------------|---------|-------------|
    %% | TIER_MEDIUM                 | LLM reasoning before dispatch    | ~2K     | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | TIER_HIGH                   | LLM planning before dispatch     | ~8K     | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | DISPATCHING (MED/HIGH)      | Preliminary ack generation       | ~200    | REALTIME    |
    %% | DELIVERING (LOW)            | Response with tool result        | ~500    | REALTIME    |
    %% | DELIVERING (MED/HIGH)       | Final response + all results     | 2-8K    | REALTIME    |
    %% | CLARIFYING                  | Generate clarification question  | ~300    | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | STAGE1_SKETCH               | LLM-powered plan sketching       | ~2K     | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | STAGE2_EXPAND               | Tool mapping & expansion         | ~1K     | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | STAGE3_VALIDATE             | LLM arbiter validation           | ~500    | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | REQUIREMENT_CLARIFICATION   | HIL clarification question       | ~300    | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | PLAN_APPROVAL               | HIL approval options format      | ~400    | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | EXECUTION_MONITORING        | Progress narration               | ~200    | BACKGROUND  |
    %% | FALLBACK_TRIGGER            | HIL question generation          | ~400    | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | SOLUTION_VALIDATOR          | Plan correctness validation      | ~500    | INTERACTIVE |
    %% | CURIOSITY_AGENT             | Gap question formulation         | ~300    | BACKGROUND  |
    %% | PROACTIVE_DECISION          | Proactive content generation     | ~500    | BACKGROUND  |
    %% | MEMORY_WRITER_AGENTS        | Memory summarization             | ~1K     | BACKGROUND  |
    %% | DYNAMIC_AGENTS              | Agent-specific LLM calls         | Variable| Variable    |
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% HEURISTIC-ONLY (No LLM): EMOTIONAL_PROCESSING, NARRATIVE_WEAVING, ANTICIPATORY_RESPONSE
    %% These compute metrics from SessionState history, not LLM calls
    %% ======================================================================================

    %% ======================================================================================
    %% BIDIRECTIONAL MESSAGE FLOW MATRIX
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% USER → SYSTEM (Inbound):
    %% | Entry Point         | Event                           | Destination           |
    %% |---------------------|----------------------------------|-----------------------|
    %% | User message        | k1.concierge.user_input         | LISTENING → ACKING    |
    %% | Interrupt           | k1.concierge.user_input         | INTERRUPT_HANDLING    |
    %% | Clarification reply | user_response                    | CLARIFYING → ACKING   |
    %% | HIL approval        | user.approval                    | PLAN_APPROVAL         |
    %% | HIL clarification   | user.clarification               | REQUIREMENT_CLARIF... |
    %% | Execution override  | user.override                    | EXECUTION_MONITORING  |
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% SYSTEM → USER (Outbound via OUTPUT_CHANNEL):
    %% | Source                    | Event                           | Priority   |
    %% |---------------------------|----------------------------------|------------|
    %% | DELIVERING                | k1.response.final.v1             | REALTIME   |
    %% | COMPANIONING              | k1.response.ack.v1               | REALTIME   |
    %% | CLARIFYING                | k1.response.clarification.v1     | REALTIME   |
    %% | PROGRESSING               | k1.response.progress.v1          | PROGRESS   |
    %% | REQUIREMENT_CLARIFICATION | k1.hil.clarification.v1          | REALTIME   |
    %% | PLAN_APPROVAL             | k1.hil.approval_request.v1       | REALTIME   |
    %% | EXECUTION_MONITORING      | k1.hil.progress.v1               | PROGRESS   |
    %% | FALLBACK_TRIGGER          | k1.hil.fallback.v1               | REALTIME   |
    %% | CURIOSITY_AGENT           | k1.proactive.question.v1         | BACKGROUND |
    %% | PROACTIVE_DECISION        | k1.proactive.message.v1          | BACKGROUND |
    %% ======================================================================================

    %% ======================================================================================
    %% INTERNAL FLOW MATRIX: Concierge → Orchestrator → Planner → Tools
    %% ======================================================================================
    %% CONCIERGE FSM CONTROL:
    %%   CONCIERGE_FSM manages state transitions for all FSM states (LISTENING, ACKING, etc.)
    %%   Single Writer pattern: Only Concierge writes to SessionState
    %%
    %% COMPLEXITY-BASED ROUTING (from DISPATCHING):
    %% | Tier   | Path                                                    | Latency   |
    %% |--------|---------------------------------------------------------|-----------|
    %% | LOW    | DISPATCHING → CAPABILITY_FABRIC → COMPANIONING          | <2s       |
    %% | MEDIUM | DISPATCHING → ORCHESTRATOR → CAPABILITY_FABRIC          | 2-10s     |
    %% | HIGH   | DISPATCHING → ORCHESTRATOR → PLANNER → CAPABILITY_FABRIC| 10-60s    |
    %%
    %% MESSAGE ENVELOPES:
    %% | Sender     | Receiver     | Envelope                               |
    %% |------------|--------------|----------------------------------------|
    %% | DISPATCHING| ORCHESTRATOR | TaskEnvelope{intent, context, tier}    |
    %% | ORCHESTRATOR| PLANNER     | PlanRequest{intent, constraints}       |
    %% | PLANNER    | ORCHESTRATOR | CommittedPlan{steps[], dependencies}   |
    %% | ORCHESTRATOR| FABRIC      | CapabilityRequest{name, params, ctx}   |
    %% | FABRIC     | ORCHESTRATOR | CapabilityResult{success, data, error} |
    %%
    %% PLAN EXECUTION:
    %%   STAGE4_COMMIT → CommittedPlan → ORCHESTRATOR → PARALLEL_DAG → CAPABILITY_FABRIC
    %%   Each step in plan.steps[] spawns tools via Fabric
    %%   Results aggregate back through PARALLEL_DAG → ORCHESTRATOR → COMPANIONING
    %% ======================================================================================

